    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate relying on the speed-oriented profile of **Nasim Nunez**, who stands as our highest-rated play at 64.14. Facing Ryan Feltner (xERA 5.10), **Nasim Nunez** benefits from a massive 19% boost due to the favorable SP matchup; given the scarcity of stolen bases in our 5x5 format, his ability to capitalize on Feltner\u2019s high-walk, high-contact profile makes him an essential start. **Sam Antonacci** (59.34) also profiles as a high-value play out of the leadoff spot against Kumar Rocker. While Rocker\u2019s pedigree is notable, the combination of **Sam Antonacci**\u2019s leadoff priority (+10%) and a positive platoon split (+7%) elevates his floor significantly, making him the primary engine for runs in today\u2019s configuration.\n\nElsewhere, the volatility of the lineup is highlighted by **Jackson Merrill** and **Tommy White**, both hovering in the mid-50s. **Jackson Merrill** faces the toughest task today against Braxton Ashcraft (xERA 3.28), where the SP skill penalty of -18% is only partially mitigated by a favorable platoon split (+13%). Conversely, **Tommy White** benefits from a +10% park factor, which helps stabilize his utility despite a marginal platoon matchup. We have opted to bench our elite core of **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Luis Robert Jr.** today, though that was forced by a team-wide off-day rather than performance, as these players remain the heart of our roster alongside the capable **Miguel Vargas** (54.64), who holds steady in the #3 spot against Rocker.\n\nInvestors should monitor the \"Lineup Pending\" status for all starters, particularly **Liam Hicks** (49.04), whose reliance on an assumed #4 slot is the biggest variable in his projection. A late shift down the batting order would dampen his value, especially against a crafty veteran like Framber Valdez. We are also tracking the status of our depth pieces like **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Drake Baldwin**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, **Curtis Mead**, **Dominic Smith**, **Wade Meckler**, and **Luis Lara** to ensure we aren't leaving potential stolen base upside on the table if late-breaking lineup news confirms better matchups for our bench. Proceed with caution on **Liam Hicks** until the official card is posted.",
